direction: down

title: |md
  ## Socket write path: where the bytes go
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

write: "send() / write()\n\nUserspace places bytes in the syscall args.\nKernel does: sock_sendmsg → tcp_sendmsg" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
}

queue: "sk_write_queue (per socket)\n\ntcp_sendmsg copies bytes from user into\nkernel skbs, appended to sk->sk_write_queue.\n\nConstraints:\n- sk->sk_sndbuf limits queued bytes\n- Cgroup memory accounting\n- skbs may merge for efficiency" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
}

cwnd: "tcp_write_xmit decides what to send NOW\n\nWalks the queue, decides per-skb:\n- Is congestion window open? (tcp_cwnd_test)\n- Is send window open? (tcp_snd_wnd_test)\n- Is Nagle satisfied?\n- TSO segment size?\n\nSends what it can; leaves the rest for later\n(next ACK, RTO, app push, ...)" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
}

xmit: "tcp_transmit_skb → ip_queue_xmit → ...\n\nHeader build, IP output, neighbor resolve,\nqdisc enqueue, driver xmit.\n\nSee bottom of full TX flow." {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
}

write -> queue -> cwnd -> xmit
